<!--
  Everything the affordance side puts in a player is only ever reached by reflection or by the
  engine, so the managed stripper sees types nobody calls and removes them. Measured at High: the
  attribute, the assembly that declares it, and the scan itself were all gone from the build, while
  the evidence resource stayed. A build that still compiles and still runs then reports a game with
  nothing in it, which is the hardest kind of loss to notice.

  Whether this file is honoured has not been confirmed — the linker command line for a High-stripped
  build named only Unity's own generated preserve files. The check in ManagedStrippingWarning is
  what makes the failure say so either way; that check arrives with ARTEL-395.

  Artel.Affordances.Scan is preserved too once it exists. It is left out here rather than written
  ahead of time because what the linker does with a name that resolves to no assembly has not been
  checked, and this file is not the place to find out. Added by ARTEL-394.
-->
<linker>
  <assembly fullname="Artel.Affordances.Runtime" preserve="all"/>
</linker>
